     "Dear list,<p>Hi. In the list at the bottom of the message I put some data about plant <br>volumes and weights in 2 maize genotypes (I have several more, but <br>putting only 2 will be enough for the example). By using &#39;dlply&#39; I fit <br>one linear model relating weight1~volume1 to each genotype, and them <br>extracted the coefficients with &#39;ldply&#39;.<p>I want to calculate a new variable based on the &#39;volume2&#39; values by <br>using the coefficients of each fitted model,(e.g. weight2 = Intercept + <br>slope*volume2).<p>As I am newly in plyr I don&#39;t know how to do it, but I guess it is <br>possible. Can someone help me with this?<p>Thanks in advance,<p>Alan.<p>################################################<br>library(plyr)<br>allometry &lt;- structure(list(rep = c(1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L,<br>1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L,<br>1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L,<br>1L, 1L, 1L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L,<br>2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L,<br>2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L,<br>3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L,<br>3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L,<br>3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 1L, 1L, 1L,<br>1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L,<br>1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L,<br>1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L,<br>2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L,<br>2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L,<br>2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 2L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L,<br>3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L,<br>3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L, 3L,<br>3L, 3L, 3L, 3L), genotype = c(1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1L,<br>1L, 1L, 1L, 1L, 1