    [
     2,
     "<p>&gt; El 16/06/2010 12:50 a.m., David Winsemius escribió:<br>&gt;&gt;<br>&gt;&gt; On Jun 14, 2010, at 5:26 PM, Alan Severini wrote:<br>&gt;&gt;<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; Dear list,<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; Hi. In the list at the bottom of the message I put some data about<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; plant volumes and weights in 2 maize genotypes (I have several more,<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; but putting only 2 will be enough for the example). By using  <br>&gt;&gt;&gt; &#39;dlply&#39; I<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; fit one linear model relating weight1~volume1 to each genotype, and<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; them extracted the coefficients with &#39;ldply&#39;.<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; I want to calculate a new variable based on the &#39;volume2&#39; values by<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; using the coefficients of each fitted model,(e.g. weight2 =  <br>&gt;&gt;&gt; Intercept<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; + slope*volume2).<br>&gt;&gt;<br>&gt;&gt; What &quot;volume2&quot;?<br>&gt;&gt;<br>&gt;&gt;&gt;<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; As I am newly in plyr I don&#39;t know how to do it, but I guess it is<br>&gt;&gt;&gt; possible. Can someone help me with this?<br>&gt;&gt;<br>&gt;&gt; Perhaps using this a a model of how to step through a dataframe:<br>&gt;&gt;<br>&gt;&gt; apply(ldply(models, coef), 1, function(x) list(Int = x[2],  <br>&gt;&gt; volcoef=x[3]))<br>&gt;&gt;<br></p>"
    ],
    [
     1,
     "<p>&gt; Thanks David. &#39;volume2&#39; is the last variable in the right part of  <br>&gt; the dataframe.<br>&gt;<br>&gt; I&#39;ve been able to extract the model coefficients by using apply (as  <br>&gt; you mention), but still I have no idea about how to use those  <br>&gt; coefficients to calculate a new variable (e.g. &#39;weight2&#39;) using  <br>&gt; &#39;volume2&#39; as input (i.e. weight2 = Intercept + slope*volume2).<p>When you ran the code you got coefficients from two models:<br> &gt; str(ldply(models, coef))<br>&#39;data.frame&#39;:\t2 obs. of  3 variables:<br>  $ genotype   : int  1 2<br>  $ (Intercept): num  3.84 5.31<br>  $ volume1    : num  0.951 0.935<p>How do you intend to use &quot;slope&quot;, which I do not see calculated with  <br>any R expressions, as applied to a vector of 270 values of &quot;volume2&quot;?   <br>My half-assed guess: Are you trying to use the value of the &quot;volume1&quot;  <br>and &#39;(Intercept)&#39; coefs in that resultant dataframe for calculation of  <br>an estimated weight on the basis of the &quot;genotype&quot; and &#39;volume2&#39;  <br>values in the original dataframe? So maybe my question should have  <br>been &quot;What slope?&quot;<p>Perhaps:<p>mod.rslt &lt;- ldply(models, coef)<br>allometry$weight2 &lt;- apply(allometry, 1, function(x) {<br>                  mod.rslt[ x[2],&#39;(Intercept)&#39;] + # choosing the  <br>(Intercept)<br>                                                 # on basis of   <br>&quot;genotype&quot; in allometry<br>                  mod.rslt[ x[2],&#39;volume1&#39;]*x[7] })  # same for what I  <br>am guessing is<br>                                                 # meant by &quot;slope&quot;.<p><br>&gt; Thanks for your help,<br>&gt;<br>&gt; Alan.<br>&gt; Aviso:<br>&gt; ======</p></p></p></p></p></p>"
